# Build output.
/target/

# The mutation gate's configuration and state.
#
# **This machine's global gitignore excludes `noha.yaml` and `.noha/`**, and had been doing so
# silently: the block below already said the baseline and the TIA table were kept, and neither had
# ever been committed. `tests/integrity.rs` reads `noha.yaml` and compares its source list against
# the tree in both directions, so without it that test cannot run from a clone at all — which is
# the strongest argument for the file being in the repository rather than beside it.
#
# A negation in a repository's own `.gitignore` outranks `core.excludesFile`, which is why these
# work. `!.noha/` has to come before the two directories below it: git will not re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so the directory is un-excluded first and its scratch is
# excluded again after.
!noha.yaml
!.noha/

# The mutation tester's scratch, which is genuinely temporary. `.noha/baseline.tsv` is the floor a
# run is measured against and `.noha/tia.tsv` is which test kills which mutant; both are worth more
# to a reader who can see them than they cost in diff noise.
.noha/work/
.noha/tmp/

# A memory store belonging to an MCP server that happens to run in this directory. Not part of the
# project, and its lock file is held open for as long as that server lives — which is also why
# `noha prober` cannot walk this tree while the server is running.
mnema.store
mnema.store.key
mnema.store.lock
